11-19","zh":"菲利普莫里斯國際公司（NYSE：PM）為何現在提高指引？"},{"title":"What Philip Morris International Doubters Overlooked","src":"Simply Wall St","url":"https://news.google.?oc=5","date":"2026-11-19","zh":"菲利普莫里斯國際公司的懷疑論者忽略了什麼"},{"title":"Once Upon A Farm sales rise 34.9% despite $30M Tractor Wheels recall costs","src":"Pluang","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqwFBVV95cUxNVEhLX3NWTGdRN3ljZ3M5N2JSZWdaN3VtLUhiem9EcXJKZXZYSUdaYzA4ZUx3VjFwM2ZyY2drWHFJTWN4SVlCbm56ZU0tdGNUOUQ3cDZUWHlQSTM3UWNyWHRlSm9KeFZMMTZPZnhwMnQxWjFqNzN6dnhNaXA0bUVLWkpfNGNDWmsySHR6TnJjTV8wVXk4RUVkWUxHNDdFejNncHdYekJNcVVyazQ?oc=5","date":"2026-11-19","zh":"儘管拖拉機車輪召回成本高達 3000 萬美元，Once Upon A Farm 銷售額仍增長 34.9%"}],"themes":[{"name":"財報","count":4},{"name":"AI 人工智慧","count":1},{"name":"股票回購/股利","count":1},{"name":"分析師評等","count":1}],"biz":{"tenk":{"form":"10-K","date":"2026-02-06","period":"2025-12-31","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1413329/000162828026005939/pm-20251231.htm"},"overview":[{"en":"Philip Morris International Inc. is a Virginia holding company incorporated in 1987. In March 2008, we became a U.S. public company listed on the New York Stock Exchange and subject to the rules of the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (the \"SEC\"). We are a leading international consumer goods company, actively delivering a smoke-free future and evolving our portfolio for the long term to include products outside of the tobacco and nicotine sector. Our current product portfolio primarily consists of cigarettes and smoke-free products, including heat-not-burn, nicotine pouch and e-vapor products. Since 2008, we have invested over $16 billion to develop, scientifically substantiate and commercialize innovative smoke-free products for adults who would otherwise continue to smoke, with the goal of completely ending the sale of cigarettes. This investment includes the building of world-","zh":"菲利普莫里斯國際公司是一家成立於 1987 年的維吉尼亞州控股公司。 2008 年 3 月，我們成為在紐約證券交易所上市的美國上市公司，並遵守美國證券交易委員會（「SEC」）的規則。我們是一家領先的國際消費品公司，積極打造無菸未來，並長期發展我們的產品組合，將菸草和尼古丁產業以外的產品納入其中。我們目前的產品組合主要包括捲菸和無菸產品，包括加熱不燃燒、尼古丁袋和電子煙產品。自 2008 年以來，我們已投資超過 160 億美元，為原本會繼續吸菸的成年人開發、科學證實和商業化創新無菸產品，目標是徹底終止香菸銷售。這項投資包括建設世界級"},{"en":"With a strong foundation and significant expertise in life sciences, PMI has a long-term ambition to expand into wellness areas. The business strategy of our wellness unit, Aspeya, currently focuses on developing and commercializing primarily oral consumer wellness offerings. This includes medical and non-recreational cannabinoid products (including CBD), in line with applicable regulatory requirements, though any revenue related to cannabinoids is expected to be negligible in the near to medium term.","zh":"憑藉著在生命科學領域的堅實基礎和豐富的專業知識，PMI 有著擴展到健康領域的長期雄心。我們的健康部門 Aspeya 的商業策略目前專注於主要口服消費者健康產品的開發和商業化。這包括符合適用監管要求的醫療和非娛樂大麻素產品（包括 CBD），儘管與大麻素相關的任何收入在中短期內預計可以忽略不計。"},{"en":"Smoke-Free Business (\"SFB\") is the term PMI uses to refer to all of its smoke-free products. SFB also includes wellness products, as well as consumer accessories, such as lighters and matches.","zh":"無菸業務（“SFB”）是 PMI 用來指稱其所有無菸產品的術語。 SFB 還包括健康產品以及消費配件，例如打火機和火柴。"}],"markets":[],"customers":[{"en":"As described in more detail in \"Distribution & Sales\" above, in many of our markets we sell our products to distributors. In 2025, sales to a distributor in the Europe Region and a distributor in the EA, AU & PMI GTR Region each amounted to 10 percent or more of our consolidated net revenues. See Item 8, Note 11. Segment Reporting for more information. We believe that none of our business segments is dependent upon a single customer or a few customers, the loss of which would have a material adverse effect on our consolidated results of operations. In some of our markets, particularly in the Europe, SSEA, CIS & MEA, and EA, AU & PMI GTR Regions, a loss of a distributor may result in a temporary market disruption.","zh":"正如上面“分銷和銷售”中更詳細地描述的，在我們的許多市場中，我們向分銷商銷售我們的產品。到 2025 年，歐洲地區經銷商以及 EA、AU 和 PMI GTR 地區經銷商的銷售額分別達到我們合併淨收入的 10% 或更多。有關詳細資訊，請參閱第 8 項註釋 11：分部報告。我們相信，我們的業務部門都不依賴單一客戶或少數客戶，失去這些客戶將對我們的綜合經營業績產生重大不利影響。在我們的一些市場，特別是歐洲、SSEA、獨聯體和中東和非洲以及 EA、AU 和 PMI GTR 區域，經銷商的流失可能會導致暫時的市場混亂。"},{"en":"Our Workforce. At December 31, 2025, we employed approximately 84,900 people worldwide, including full-time, temporary and part-time staff. Our businesses are subject to a number of laws and regulations relating to our relationship with our employees. Generally, these laws and regulations are specific to the location of each business. We engage with legally recognized employee representative bodies and we have collective bargaining agreements in several of the countries in which we operate. In addition, in accordance with E.U. requirements, we have established a European Works Council composed of management and elected members of our workforce. We believe we maintain good relations with our employees and their representative organizations.","zh":"我們的員工團隊。截至 2025 年 12 月 31 日，我們在全球僱用了約 84,900 名員工，包括全職、臨時和兼職員工。我們的業務受到與我們與員工關係相關的多項法律和法規的約束。一般來說，這些法律和法規針對每個企業所在地。我們與法律認可的員工代表機構合作，並在我們開展業務的多個國家/地區簽訂了集體談判協議。此外，根據 EU.根據要求，我們建立了一個由管理階層和當選的員工組成的歐洲工作委員會。我們相信我們與員工及其代表組織保持著良好的關係。"}],"competition":[{"en":"We are subject to highly competitive conditions in all aspects of our business. We compete primarily on the basis of product quality, brand recognition, brand loyalty, taste, R&D, innovation, packaging, customer service, marketing, advertising and retail price.","zh":"我們業務的各個方面都面臨著高度競爭的條件。我們的競爭主要基於產品品質、品牌認知、品牌忠誠度、品味、研發、創新、包裝、客戶服務、行銷、廣告和零售價格。"},{"en":"The competitive environment and our competitive position can be significantly influenced by weak economic conditions; erosion of consumer confidence; competitors' introduction of lower-price products or innovative products; adult smoker willingness to convert to our SFPs; higher product taxes; higher absolute prices and larger gaps between retail price categories; and product regulation that diminishes the ability to differentiate products, restricts adult consumer access to truthful and non-misleading information about our SFPs, or disproportionately impacts the commercialization of our products in relation to our competitors.","zh":"競爭環境和我們的競爭地位可能會受到疲軟的經濟狀況的顯著影響；消費者信心受到侵蝕；競爭對手推出低價產品或創新產品；成年吸煙者願意轉用我們的 SFP；更高的產品稅；絕對價格較高，零售價格類別之間的差距較大；產品監管削弱了產品差異化的能力，限製成年消費者獲取有關我們的 SFP 的真實影響力的資訊相對我們的真實性，或者對於商業化的資訊相對我們的 SFP 的真實影響不成比例。"}],"segments":{"seg":{"end":"2025-12-31","items":[{"name":"Europe","val":17111000000,"zh":"歐洲"},{"name":"SSEACISMEA","val":12051000000,"zh":"SSEACISMEA 分部"},{"name":"EAAUPMIGTR","val":6632000000,"zh":"EAAUPMIGTR 段"},{"name":"Americas","val":4854000000,"zh":"美洲"}],"total":40648000000},"prod":{"end":"2025-12-31","items":[{"name":"Combustible Tobacco Products","val":23794000000,"zh":"可燃煙草製品"},{"name":"Smoke Free Products","val":16854000000,"zh":"無菸產品"}],"total":40648000000}},"peers":["MO","MDLZ","KHC","PEP","KMB"]}}